+
+The place's other SurfaceGuis (the store and dealership signs: 2) are not counted above.
+
+## 5. Navigation: does every junction need a sign?
+**No.**
+
+**The navigation targets are few:**
+- spawn on the central plaza;
+- the 24/7 MART on B Ave (x = −100) between z = −100 and 100;
+- OUTLAW MOTORS on 3rd St (z = 100), east of C Ave;
+- the highway via the two connectors north of z = −300.
+
+**What each stage gives:**
+- **A (the four plaza-ring junctions)** names every road a player uses between spawn, the store and the dealership.
+- **B (the two connectors)** names the way to and from the highway.
+- **Stages C and D** sit on the perimeter, where the grid itself is easy to read and traffic is light.
+
+**Recommendation:** stop after B (6 signs). Do C only if owner playtest feedback shows people get lost at the edges, and don't do D.
+
+## 6. Naming alternatives (owner decision; the prototype keeps "3rd St" / "C Ave")
+**Length limit:** names must stay short. `TextScaled` shrinks long names to fit the 7-stud blade, and the measured glyph height is only 5–7 px at about 60 studs on desktop with 5–6 characters. Keep names to 8 characters or fewer.
+
+| Road | Plain grid (extends the prototype) | Themed (OUTLAW CITY) | Why the themed name |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| z = −300 (by the highway) | 1st St | Rail St | Edge of town, towards the highway |
+| z = −100 | 2nd St | Gold St | Passes the robbable 24/7 MART side |
+| z = 100 | 3rd St | Main St | Plaza front and OUTLAW MOTORS |
+| z = 300 (towards the jail) | 4th St | Iron St | Nearest the jail |
+| x = −300 | A Ave | Colt Ave | West edge, "Old Town" (brick) district |
+| x = −100 | B Ave | Mesa Ave | The 24/7 MART avenue |
+| x = 100 | C Ave | Dust Ave | Downtown avenue to the dealership |
+| x = 300 | D Ave | Spur Ave | East edge |
+
+**Plain names:**
+- predictable, ordered by position, so they help mental mapping;
+- they match the approved prototype, so no change is needed.
+
+**Themed names:**
+- carry more flavour;
+- adopting them would rename the prototype (a separate, approved change);
+- they give no order cue.
+
+**My recommendation:** plain names for the rollout.
+
+## 7. Staged rollout
+### Stage A (first implementation batch, recommended)
+**Signs:**
+- (−100, −100), corner (−,−), post (−122, 0.6, −122): "2nd St" / "B Ave";
+- (100, −100), corner (+,+), post (122, 0.6, −78): "2nd St" / "C Ave";
+- (−100, 100), corner (−,−), post (−122, 0.6, 78): "3rd St" / "B Ave".
+
+**How:**
+1. **Backup first.** The owner saves the place and I check the Studio log.
+2. **Data:** add three entries to `CityLayout.STREET_SIGNS` (`{X, Z, CornerX, CornerZ}`). No new code: the builder and the cantilever rule already handle any corner.
+3. **Studio:** these are new model names, so `buildStreetSigns` adds exactly these three and skips the approved one. The prototype is untouched; I verify its signature `87d79268` stays.
+4. **Spec:** generalise the one-sign tests to every entry. For each sign check:
+   - 3 parts and 4 labels;
+   - full footprints on one sidewalk;
+   - post face 3.8 and blades 3.9 from the road;
+   - at least 3 studs from buildings, store and dealership;
+   - no overlap with markings;
+   - cantilever with no shared volume;
+   - names from the tables.
+
+   Also check that the total count is 4 and there are no duplicate names.
+
+**Desktop acceptance:**
+- BaseParts 328, colliding 114.
+- City `6527bae1`, stop-line `f958ecfa`, 186-part `8b66ade9` and prototype `87d79268` unchanged.
+- All tests pass.
+- For each new sign: the 4 incoming-approach captures (2 each) plus one 30-stud reading view per served approach. Every name is complete (no occlusion); the weak approach is recorded as expected.
+- Drive past each new sign in all lanes (no bump); walk through each post (no touch).
+- Police bust/jail, robbery, vehicle spawn and dealership regressions.
+- FPS and memory: 3 idle + 3 pursuit before and after, Studio in front. Memory alternating in fresh sessions, as in the N5 closeout.
+- **Pass:** 60 fps held, with no reproducible hitch. Memory change within the session noise band, otherwise reported as INCONCLUSIVE, not passed.
+
+**Phone simulator plan:**
+- The owner switches on Studio's Device Simulator (iPhone 7 666 × 374 and one larger phone).
+- I capture the same 30 and 60-stud views and read idle FPS facing the plaza ring.
+- **Pass:** names readable at 30 studs. The 60-stud result is recorded either way.
+- If the simulator isn't available, the check is marked **PHONE SIMULATOR NOT TESTED**; desktop captures are not substituted. A real phone stays NOT TESTED.
+
+**Streaming and duplicates:**
+- On the client: each new model is Atomic, with 3 parts and 4 GUIs present when in range.
+- One sign per name after a server restart, two extra builder calls and a fresh full rebuild.
+
+**Rollback:**
+- Remove the three entries and delete the three new models.
+- Must return exactly: 319 / 114, prototype signature `87d79268`, 215 tests. This is shown in Studio before sign-off.
+
+### Go / no-go gate before Stage B
+Proceed only if **all** hold:
+1. Every Stage A acceptance item passes, or is marked NOT TESTED with the reason.
+2. No letter is occluded on any new face.
+3. No reproducible FPS regression.
+4. Rollback is demonstrated exactly.
+5. The phone-simulator result is recorded, or explicitly NOT TESTED.
+6. The owner has played and says the signs help.
+7. The Architect approves.
+
+Stage B (connectors, 2 signs) then repeats the same acceptance with its own gate. Stages C and D each need their own approval and are not recommended now.
+
+## 8. Rollback (any stage)
+Delete the stage's entries from `STREET_SIGNS` and their models from `City.StreetSigns`. The builder never recreates removed entries. Earlier stages and the approved prototype stay intact.
+
+## 9. Not in this plan
+- Building any sign.
+- Signs at the connector–highway joins (±100, −492).
+- Second signs on opposite corners.
+- New markings or roads.
+- Renaming the prototype.
